{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^#|D726|D756|D757|D758'\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md | tail -45\"","aggregated_output":"10859:## D721 · 2026-11-22 · Council round 43/43b: the double-count premise is partly falsified by the frozen gold; recommend closing the design with nothing to build; D711's H4 reading corrected\n10892:## D722 · 2026-11-22 · Alex closes the double-count design with nothing changed\n10905:## D723 · 2026-11-22 · Code review of 95cf8da7..3ba40d8f: two defects fixed, eight findings recorded\n10931:## D724 · 2026-11-22 · Council round 44 converges the code review: keep the v12 launcher refusal and the clean-ups, revert the link-step catch; D723 corrected\n10957:## D725 · 2026-11-22 · Council round 45/45b: the number answers fail because related numbers have no shared, checked calculation; one judge version and one test recommended to Alex\n10991:## D726 · 2026-11-22 · Alex opens a judge version for related number questions ($0 gate first) and agrees to \"Forecast unavailable\" as the first-release interim\n11008:## D727 · 2026-11-22 · judging-v13's $0 gate: the design passed council (round 46e); gate runs 1–6 and council rounds 46f–46j; the gate is not yet passed; one choice goes to Alex\n11041:## D728 · 2026-11-22 · Alex: the family judge does not see its earlier forecasts while calculating\n11055:## D729 · 2026-11-22 · judging-v13's $0 gate passes (council round 46ad); the paid gate needs its harness built at $0 and Alex's ceiling\n11073:## D730 · 2026-11-22 · Alex: build the paid gate's harness at $0, then ask for the ceiling\n11083:## D731 · 2026-11-22 · judging-v13's paid-gate harness is ready to send (council round 47h); the first attempt is scored on both arms; the ceiling is Alex's\n11110:## D732 · 2026-11-22 · Alex: the paid gate's ceiling is $0.50\n11122:## D733 · 2026-11-22 · judging-v13's paid gate: STOP, every answer refused; the format's rules were never stated in the request (council round 48); repair or close is Alex's choice\n11169:## D734 · 2026-11-22 · Alex: repair judging-v13's request and checks once, then a $0 blind conformance test\n11185:## D735 · 2026-11-22 · Council rounds 49–50: the repair is finished to a line; at most two more review rounds, then the blind test\n11210:## D736 · 2026-11-22 · Council round 51: the repair's wording review finds as many serious issues as round 49; Claude and Codex split on going back to Alex now\n11236:## D737 · 2026-11-22 · Alex: shrink judging-v13's format to the checks that stop the named defects, then a $0 blind test\n11258:## D738 · 2026-11-22 · v13s: code refuses a named defect only where the calculation's structure decides it; readers mark the five defects on every reply (council rounds 52–53)\n11290:## D739 · 2026-11-22 · v13s built and rehearsed; council round 54's findings fixed; the blind test runs, and its result goes to Council B\n11325:## D740 · 2026-11-22 · The v13s blind test stops on a checker error and a reader-marked defect; council round 55 sends three reader rulings to Alex\n11346:## D741 · 2026-11-22 · Alex rules the three reader questions of D740\n11369:## D742 · 2026-11-22 · The v13s re-run stops on one sound answer refused by S4; council 56–56c keeps S4 and makes the request state one benchmark rule; a third $0 blind run follows\n11416:## D743 · 2026-11-22 · The third v13s blind run stops on the reader brief; the writer side is clean; council 57 asks Alex to authorize a re-reading\n11449:## D744 · 2026-11-22 · The D743 re-read fixes the range rule but stops on the midpoint; one mechanism (readers lack the writer's format rules); council 58 asks Alex for one more bounded re-read under shared rule text\n11484:## D745 · 2026-11-23 · The D744 re-read calibrates the readers but stops on a qualifier-list gap and on S's unsupported share; council 59 recommends a targeted $0 test of one clarification, for Alex to authorize\n11524:## D746 · 2026-11-23 · The D745 targeted test fails on E's unsized cut; S splits on how far an indirect comparison can support a forecast; council 61–61b: one general question to Alex, then a $0 stored-answer re-read; the paid re-send stays on hold\n11573:## D747 · 2026-11-23 · Alex rules that a forecast may rest on an explained indirect comparison\n11592:## D748 · 2026-11-23 · The D747 re-read fails on a self-contradicting floor; three of four earlier splits settle under the ruling; council 63: ask Alex to authorize the E writer repair; the paid re-send stays on hold\n11641:## D749 · 2026-11-23 · Alex authorizes the E writer repair and its $0 writer test\n11656:## D750 · 2026-11-23 · The D749 writer test is INCONCLUSIVE with no failed line; council 65 (under D439): one bullet-2 sentence on reaffirmed targets, then a second $0 writer test\n11683:## D751 · 2026-11-23 · D750 fails on E's bracket midpoint; council 67–68 (under D439): one structural line-9 change, a paper check first, then one last writer test with an exit rule back to Alex\n11721:## D752 · 2026-11-23 · D751 fails, so the wording loop ends under its exit rule; council 69–69b: two questions to Alex (the E-type publication default, agreed; the paid re-send, split)\n11754:## D753 · 2026-11-23 · Alex chooses \"can't tell yet\" as the E-type default and a one-time paid exception\n11775:## D754 · 2026-11-23 · The one-time v13s paid re-send is prepared, reviewed in council 70–70c, and sent under Alex's D753\n11799:## D755 · 2026-11-23 · The paid re-send STOPs (complete); council 71: close v13s at STOP and carry D726's \"Forecast unavailable\" into the first release\n11814:  - the first release carries D726: number questions show their sources and \"Forecast unavailable\", with the range, forecast text and\n11823:## D756 · 2026-11-23 · Alex closes the v13s line; the first release shows number questions as \"Forecast unavailable\"\n11833:  - The first release carries D726: number questions show the question and its sources with \"Forecast unavailable\", the band, the\n11842:## D757 · 2026-11-23 · Toward production: the \"Forecast unavailable\" release design is ready for when Alex opens release work (council 72–72d); two choices go to Alex\n11845:  unavailable\" (D756). D726 says it \"is built with the release work, which is not started\". Council 72 agreed that opening release\n11867:## D758 · 2026-11-23 · Under D439 the council opens local release work for \"Forecast unavailable\"; non-number questions show no explanation text (§4 a); the v13s checker defects are closed as won't-fix (council 73)\n11870:  Production 方向去走了\"). He had already chosen the behaviour (D726 \"同意\"; D756 \"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线\"). D757 left two\n11875:     can be deleted without touching what the POC serves. D726's \"not started\" described the state on 2026-11-22 and set no gate.\n11880:     code, the line is closed (D756), and the STOP bars tuning on the 36 answers. The findings stay on record.\n11881:  4. **Order:** the exporter and the checked package first; the reader's screen second (it completes D756's screen check). How the\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
