{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round74-brief.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Council round 74: review the slice-1 build design before any code (read-only)\n     2\t\n     3\tYou are an independent reviewer. Do not edit any file. The repository is /Users/lchingen/hivemind. Cite file:line.\n     4\t\n     5\t## What to review\n     6\t\n     7\t`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md`, the build design for the first slice of the \"Forecast unavailable\"\n     8\trelease. The governing documents:\n     9\t- `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md` (revision 4, ready per `codex-r72d.md`);\n    10\t- D726, D756, D757 and D758 at the end of `docs/DECISIONS-log.md`;\n    11\t- AGENTS.md §2 (design tables before code), §3 (one owner; the writer refuses), §4 (tests) and §5.\n    12\t\n    13\tCode that the design reuses:\n    14\t- `src/hivemind/service.py`: `resolve_bound`, `view_exists`, `is_open_as_of`, `state_as_of`, `evidence`, `evidence_record`,\n    15\t  `ladder_bands`;\n    16\t- `src/hivemind/bundle.py`: `read_snapshot`, `item_lookup`, `view_bundle`;\n    17\t- `src/hivemind/views/store.py`: `view_key`, `rungs_of`;\n    18\t- `src/hivemind/views/identity.py:10`;\n    19\t- `src/hivemind/vocabulary.py:24`;\n    20\t- `src/hivemind/idea.py`, for the idea question.\n    21\t\n    22\t## Questions\n    23\t\n    24\t1. **Leaks.** Does the allow-list in §1 let any number forecast reach the package? Check:\n    25\t   - each allowed field's real content in stored stores, read-only (for example `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite`):\n    26\t     `question`, evidence `one_line` and `quote`, source titles;\n    27\t   - whether evidence linked to a number question can itself be a system-written forecast rather than a source statement.\n    28\t\n    29\t   Name any path with a stored example.\n    30\t2. **Tables.** Are the state × event, value × reader and new path × old checks tables complete? Name any blank or wrong cell, for\n    31\t   example an event the export can meet that is not listed.\n    32\t3. **Tests and mutants.** Does each named test fail without the code it tests? Is a decisive case missing?\n    33\t4. **The $0 release check (§7).** Is the leak sweep sound? Consider the 12-character floor and the string classes. Would it miss a\n    34\t   forecast restated in different words?\n    35\t5. **The four open points in §8:**\n    36\t   - no idea submission in the release, with the idea acceptance moved to a later slice;\n    37\t   - `object` and `kind` on every record;\n    38\t   - groups left out;\n    39\t   - the sweep floor.\n    40\t\n    41\t   Decide each.\n    42\t6. **Ready to build?** Give a verdict: ready, or not ready with each serious finding.\n    43\t\n    44\t**Out of scope:** the judging, opening and extraction pieces (frozen); the closed v13s line; the POC's own behaviour; any other open\n    45\tdefect; wording. Report only findings that change what is built or whether it is safe.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r74.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Claude's response to council round 74 (`codex-r74.md`)\n     2\t\n     3\tI read each cited record and code line before answering.\n     4\t\n     5\t## Accepted (design revision 2)\n     6\t\n     7\t1. **The pass condition becomes an origin check, not a string sweep.** Every package field is compared with its permitted stored source\n     8\t   at the bound, read by separate direct SQL. Substituting the system's \"$390 billion\" (`old-1` j1580 `implied_outcome`) into\n     9\t   `e2295`'s summary then fails, because the summary no longer equals the stored one. The string search stays as a diagnostic on\n    10\t   decoded fields, with no floor, and every hit is attributed and read by hand.\n    11\t2. **A source whose item is missing is refused.** The release has its own item lookup with no fallback.\n    12\t3. **The staged package is checked before the rename.** A refused build removes its own staging folder and leaves no final folder. A\n    13\t   crash leaves the staging folder, and the next build refuses until it is removed. A `check` mode re-verifies an existing package and\n    14\t   rewrites its report.\n    15\t4. **The manifest is a closed set:** `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`, `data_sha256`, each cross-checked against the data.\n    16\t5. **Date validation carried over:** `date.fromisoformat` on the bound; a store with no default day is refused; a valid day before the\n    17\t   first question gives an empty package.\n    18\t6. **Narrow reads.** The exporter reads rung labels, the latest judgement's rung and the key's measure with its own column-limited\n    19\t   SQL, not `state_as_of` or `rungs_of`. The report unpacks `ladder_bands`' `(bands, reason)`.\n    20\t7. **Size and speed budgets** are set before the first control.\n    21\t8. **Tests:**\n    22\t   - fixtures that separate every branch, with a condition-only resolved number, unresolved numbers with and without a key, the\n    23\t     served ledger's \"Restriction adopted\" labels, and a legacy store with no key table;\n    24\t   - a manifest-prose mutant;\n    25\t   - a mutant that writes judgement text into `one_line`;\n    26\t   - writer refusal exercised through the builder;\n    27\t   - the known leaks exported at 2026-08-25 and 2026-08-28.\n    28\t9. **The open points:** no idea submission, its acceptance carried forward; `object` and `kind` dropped; groups out; floor removed.\n    29\t10. **The decisive acceptance case,** as stated in `codex-r74.md`. It also keeps `e3597`'s genuine $390 billion analyst quote as a\n    30\t    control.\n    31\t\n    32\t## Disputed: rewriting evidence summaries that state a calculated figure\n    33\t\n    34\t`codex-r74.md` §1 asks the release to use the source wording where a summary introduces a calculated figure (`e3238`: \"more than\n    35\t$40 billion\" from \"more than double\"). I propose keeping the summary as extraction stored it, for four reasons.\n    36\t\n    37\t- **What D726 withholds is the judge's output:** the band, the forecast text and the history (Alex: \"档位和预测文字写成'预测暂缺'\").\n    38\t  The evidence is the extraction step's reading of a source, and extraction runs on the frozen production prompt (v74i).\n    39\t- **Extraction never sees the system's forecast.** The request lists each open question only as id, object, due day, question and a\n    40\t  \"takes\" line (`src/hivemind/placement.py:59-61`, `:19-42`; `src/hivemind/extraction.py:398-400`). No rung, label or judged position\n    41\t  is shown. A summary therefore cannot echo our forecast; its figures come from the item.\n    42\t- **The measured rule would mostly remove harmless text.** \"Every number in the summary must be in the quote\" fails on 25.6%, 25.2%\n    43\t  and 25.4% of the evidence in force in `old-1`, `old-2` and `old-3`, and on 35.0% in the served ledger\n    44\t  (`scratchpad oneline_census.py`). In a random sample of 24 failures, 23 are context made explicit: a year for \"this year\", a date\n    45\t  for \"Monday\", \"Q3\", \"FY2027\", a product name such as \"H200\", an amount from the previous sentence. One (served `e2798`) restates\n    46\t  \"close to doubling\" as \"nearly 100%\". The rule would be a patch on the extraction module, which this\n    47\t  slice has not taken up (AGENTS, \"Authority and scope\").\n    48\t- **\"Amounts as quoted\"** in the design meant the release computes or converts nothing. Revision 2 says so in those words. The\n    49\t  property (a summary can restate a source figure by arithmetic, attributed to its source) is disclosed in the design, not built.\n    50\t\n    51\tIf the council still disagrees, AGENTS says to take the cheaper, reversible course. Keeping the stored summary is cheaper and is\n    52\treversible: the field can be dropped from the allow-list in a later version.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t**Verdict: not ready to build.** The proposed check would accept Hivemind’s own forecast inside an allowed text field. It would also flag genuine source material. Both failures are reproducible on `old-1/v8`: the check misses the stored forecast of about **$390 billion**, while a source quote legitimately contains the withheld label **“Bullish.”** [Release check:197](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:197) · [Evidence returned to the exporter:232](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:232)\n     2\t\n     3\t### 1. What can reach a reader\n     4\t\n     5\tI checked the three comparison stores and the served ledger read-only. I found **no confirmed case of a stored judgement being copied into an evidence record**. I did find a meaningful difference between the article, the system’s summary of it, and the system’s own answer. The build design treats all three as strings.\n     6\t\n     7\t| Stored case | What the reader would see |\n     8\t|---|---|\n     9\t| `old-1/v8/e2295` | Morningstar estimates **$361 billion**. Its quote gives that figure and its summary attributes it to Morningstar. This is precisely the evidence the release should preserve. |\n    10\t| `old-1/v15/e3238` | The quote gives **$20 billion** this year and **“more than double”** next year. The system’s one-line summary supplies **“more than $40 billion.”** That is faithful arithmetic, but the system wrote the dollar figure. |\n    11\t| `old-2/v38`, `e3877` | The article title gives **$2.5 billion**. The article says NVIDIA may provide roughly half of a **$5–6 billion** round. Both the stored *question* and the evidence summary spell out **$2.5–3 billion**. The question already contained the range before its first judgement. |\n    12\t| `old-1/v8/e5309` | The source title forecasts **$31.6 trillion** of global spending by 2050. The linked evidence concerns NVIDIA’s reported first-half revenue. The title is a publisher’s forecast and belongs with its source. |\n    13\t\n    14\tThe writer checks the quote against the article. It stores the generated `one_line` separately. Linking the two to a number question establishes neither that every amount was quoted nor that the summary contains a Hivemind judgement. Keep attributed source forecasts and the original question. For the release promise of “amounts as quoted,” use the source wording where the summary introduces a calculated figure. Verify each exported value against its designated origin. A valid key name alone cannot establish that origin. [Signed design:47](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:47) · [Quote check:671](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/extraction.py:671) · [Evidence writer:29](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/writing.py:29) · [Question writer:38](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/writing.py:38)\n    15\t\n    16\t### 2. Missing or wrong table entries\n    17\t\n    18\t| Table | What changes the build |\n    19\t|---|---|\n    20\t| State × event | **Missing source item.** `item_lookup` substitutes the input ID for the title and empty strings for publisher and URI. All pass the proposed string checks. Refuse a visible source that cannot be matched to its item. The four store/item pairs I checked had zero missing source IDs. [Lookup:28](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/bundle.py:28) · [Proposed value checks:62](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:62) |\n    21\t| State × event | **Failure after rename.** The builder puts the directory in its final location before checking the package and writing the report. A failed check leaves a final-looking directory, and a retry refuses it. Check the staged package before rename. Specify what happens if only the report fails and how the user can retry. [Build order:67](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:67) · [Crash and retry rows:100](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:100) |\n    22\t| Value × reader | **The manifest is a second place to put a forecast.** The proposed package check verifies the data hash but leaves manifest keys and agreement on `format`, `allow_list` and `as_of` unspecified. An extra forecast in `manifest.json` leaves the data hash intact. Require exactly the four manifest fields and cross-check their values. Include the report and its unresolved-question reader in the table. [Package check:69](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:69) · [Reader table:109](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:109) |\n    23\t| New path × old checks | **Date validation was lost.** `resolve_bound` compares the supplied text to the last completed day. `bundle.library` separately rejects a missing default and parses the date. An impossible date such as `2026-08-99` sorts before the comparison stores’ September 20 bound. Carry over both checks. Distinguish a missing default from a valid date before the first visible question, which can yield an empty library. [Bound:64](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:64) · [Library:227](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/bundle.py:227) |\n    24\t| Value × reader and old checks | **The named helpers do more than the table says.** `state_as_of` reads all judgement columns and decodes theme pushes. `rungs_of` reads conditions and bounds. Use a narrow label/position read for the package if the “never read” promise stands. Also unpack `ladder_bands` in the report: failure returns **`(None, reason)`**. Testing the whole return value for `None` silently misses unresolved questions. [Build claims:125](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:125) · [Judgement reader:129](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:129) · [Rung reader:97](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/store.py:97) · [Band result:499](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:499) |\n    25\t\n    26\tSection 7 also records bytes and seconds without a pass threshold. Set the size and speed budgets before the first control, as the repository requires. [Release check:209](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:209) · [AGENTS.md:120](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/AGENTS.md:120)\n    27\t\n    28\t### 3. Tests and mutants\n    29\t\n    30\tThe tests exist only on paper. Several would still pass with the intended protection removed.\n    31\t\n    32\t- **Tests 1, 2 and 7** catch an extra key or a copied passage. Add a mutant that keeps every key valid and puts the number judgement into `one_line`. Exercise the exporter through the builder. Check the exact source-backed value and confirm a refused build produces no final package. Calling `check_export` on an edited dictionary alone does not exercise the writer’s refusal. [Tests:163](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:163) · [Writer requirement:124](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/AGENTS.md:124)\n    33\t- **Tests 3, 4, 5, 6 and 11** need fixtures that distinguish the branches. Defaulting to `number` passes test 3 even if the unresolved report lists every number question. Assert a condition-only *resolved* question is absent from that report and an unresolved one is present, both with and without a key. For test 6 use the served ledger’s `v49` labels, **“Restriction adopted” / “No restriction adopted.”** All 85 comparison-store events also have Yes/No labels, so removing event recognition can leave the displayed answer unchanged. Exercise the legacy case with the key table genuinely absent. [Tests:168](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:168) · [Event overlap:85](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:85) · [Legacy lookup:159](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/store.py:159)\n    34\t- **Tests 8–10** have useful controls for evidence dates, foreign files and changed bytes. Add an unchanged-data-hash mutant with extra manifest prose. For the two known event leaks, export at **August 25** for `old-3/v36/j799` and **August 28** for `old-1/v10/j865`. I verified those are the last judgements on those dates. The default September 20 exports select **j1698** and **j1581**, so absence of the older prose there proves little. Assert the original answer label as well as the absence of the forecast. [Tests:175](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:175) · [Stored leak dates:1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72b.md:1)\n    35\t\n    36\t### 4. The $0 sweep\n    37\t\n    38\t**Reject the 12-character floor as a release gate.** On `old-1/v8` it skips three of five labels: `Bullish`, `Neutral` and `Bearish`. Removing the floor still gives a wrong result. `old-1/v8/e1865` genuinely begins its source quote with **“Bullish confirmation would require…”**. Section 7’s requirement that none of the five labels occur anywhere conflicts with preserving that quote. [Sweep and acceptance:197](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:197)\n    39\t\n    40\tI also checked the opposite error in memory. The **entire** `old-1/v8/j1580.implied_outcome`, beginning “About $390 billion,” contains **zero** of §7’s searched strings of 12 or more characters. The restatement “Our estimate for the year is $390bn” also produces zero. The sweep omits `implied_outcome`, `reference`, numeric bounds and structured judgement values. Searching serialized JSON also changes how quotation marks and newlines appear. Use exact matches on **decoded fields** as diagnostics, including short labels. Make the pass condition an independent comparison of package fields with their permitted source values at the requested date. Preserve the genuine $390 billion article quote in `old-1/e3597` as the control. [Stored judgement fields:18](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/store.py:18) · [Proposed sweep:201](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:201)\n    41\t\n    42\t### 5. Decisions on the four open points\n    43\t\n    44\t| Open point | Decision |\n    45\t|---|---|\n    46\t| Idea submission | **Defer it.** The static release should offer no submission control or route. Carry the `old-1/v8` idea-card and composed-request acceptance forward as pending for the first idea-enabled slice. D758 expressly delegates this sequencing decision. [D758:11881](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11881) · [Idea acceptance:128](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:128) |\n    47\t| `object` and `kind` | **Drop both from the first package.** D757 authorizes the question, its sources and the marker. The question ID already supplies identity. The proposed object grouping is a separate display choice. [D757:11850](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11850) · [Proposed additions:214](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:214) |\n    48\t| Research groups | **Leave them out.** They add generated names, scopes and aliases, and the agreed release screen needs none of them. [Group reader:213](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/bundle.py:213) · [D756 screen requirement:11833](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11833) |\n    49\t| Sweep floor | **Remove it as a safety criterion.** Keep diagnostic hits attributable to a particular question, field and source. [Release check:197](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:197) |\n    50\t\n    51\t**The decisive acceptance case** is one package that preserves Morningstar’s **$361 billion** estimate and the genuine **“Bullish confirmation”** quote, yet fails when Hivemind’s **$390 billion** answer is substituted into that same evidence field or added to the manifest. Revise the design around that case before coding.","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
