{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '132,320p'\"","aggregated_output":"   132\t## 2. State × event (one export, read-only)\n   133\t\n   134\t| State / event | What happens | What is written | Day used |\n   135\t|---|---|---|---|\n   136\t| Store's first day still in progress | `FirstDayNotCompleted`; the build stops | nothing | none |\n   137\t| Store with no completed day and no judgement, `--as-of` omitted | refused: \"no default day; supply --as-of\" | nothing | none |\n   138\t| `--as-of` not a valid date (`2026-08-99`) | refused by `date.fromisoformat` | nothing | none |\n   139\t| `--as-of` after the last completed day | `BoundNotCompleted`; the build stops | nothing | requested day |\n   140\t| `--as-of` valid, before the first visible question | empty `questions`; the report says 0 | package | bound |\n   141\t| `--as-of` omitted | last completed day (a legacy ledger: its last judgement day) | package | resolved bound |\n   142\t| View created after the bound | not exported | — | bound |\n   143\t| View closed on or before the bound | `open: false`, with no reason and no day | — | bound |\n   144\t| Closed, then reopened, before the bound | the last visible switch wins | — | bound |\n   145\t| Event or Yes/No not yet judged at the bound | `answer: null` | — | bound |\n   146\t| Evidence replaced on or before the bound | excluded; the replacement is in force | — | bound |\n   147\t| Evidence replaced after the bound | kept | — | bound |\n   148\t| Source recorded after the bound | excluded | — | bound |\n   149\t| Visible source with no row in the items database | `ReleaseRefused`, naming the evidence and input id | nothing final | bound |\n   150\t| Store written by a live run | not supported. The builder is given a snapshot (AGENTS §9), and both connections are pinned | — | — |\n   151\t| `--out` exists, or `<out>.staging` exists | refused before any write | nothing | — |\n   152\t| `check_export`, `check_package` or `check_origins` refuses | the staging folder is removed, exit non-zero | nothing final | — |\n   153\t| Crash while staging | the staging folder is left, and the next build refuses until it is removed | staging only | — |\n   154\t| Crash after the rename, before the report | the package is final and checked; `check` rewrites the report | package | — |\n   155\t| Two builds of one store | the second needs a new `--out` | — | — |\n   156\t| Store or configuration changed between builds | each package records its bound and data sha256; the report names the store path | — | — |\n   157\t| Legacy ledger: no `view_keys` table, `是`/`否` labels | no key, so no event; the labels canonicalise to Yes/No | — | — |\n   158\t\n   159\t## 3. Value × reader\n   160\t\n   161\tReaders of the package:\n   162\t- `check_package` and `check_origins`;\n   163\t- the release page (slice 2);\n   164\t- the tests.\n   165\t\n   166\tThe report's reader is the person building. No POC code imports `release`.\n   167\t\n   168\t| Value | Permitted source at the bound | Checked by |\n   169\t|---|---|---|\n   170\t| `id`, `question` | `views.view_id`, `views.question` | `check_origins` |\n   171\t| `open` | the latest visible `view_switches.open` | `check_origins` |\n   172\t| `class` | `view_keys.measure`, `rungs.label` | tests and mutants (identity) |\n   173\t| `answers`, `answer` | `rungs.label` by position; the latest `judgements.rung` on or before the bound | `check_origins` |\n   174\t| `forecast` | the constant marker | `check_export` |\n   175\t| evidence fields | the `evidence` row; visible `evidence_links` minus visible replacements | `check_origins` |\n   176\t| source fields | visible `evidence_sources.publication_day`; `items.title`, `publisher`, `source_uri` | `check_origins` |\n   177\t| manifest | the data's `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`; the data sha256 | `check_package` |\n   178\t| report (outside the package) | `ladder_bands` per number question; counts | read by the builder's user |\n   179\t\n   180\t**Never read by `release_export`:**\n   181\t- `rungs.condition`, `lo`, `hi`;\n   182\t- `judgements.reasons`, `why_changed`, `implied_outcome`, `reference`, `pushes_json`, `theme_pushes_json`, `cited_*`;\n   183\t- `view_switches.reason`;\n   184\t- `clean_ladders`;\n   185\t- `thesis_groups`;\n   186\t- `dependencies`, `successions`.\n   187\t\n   188\t## 4. New path × old checks\n   189\t\n   190\t| Check on the old path (`bundle.library`, `view_bundle`, `service`) | New path |\n   191\t|---|---|\n   192\t| `resolve_bound`: unfinished first day, future bound | same call |\n   193\t| `bundle.library`: no default day refused; `date.fromisoformat` | same two checks |\n   194\t| A view not visible at the bound is not served | same `view_exists` |\n   195\t| Sources visible at the bound; replacements applied | same `service.evidence`, verified independently by `check_origins` |\n   196\t| Pinned read transaction | same `bundle.read_snapshot` |\n   197\t| `item_lookup` falls back to the id for a missing item | refused instead |\n   198\t| A malformed `clean_ladders` row is refused | not read |\n   199\t| Corrupt judgement JSON is refused | no JSON column read |\n   200\t| The UI contract rejects unknown fields | the release's own `check_export`; the page's reading of it is slice 2 |\n   201\t\n   202\t## 5. Prior decisions\n   203\t\n   204\t- D726: number questions show sources and \"Forecast unavailable\", with band, forecast text and history withheld together.\n   205\t- D756: Alex's choice.\n   206\t- D757: the design, revision 4.\n   207\t- D758: the release is opened; §4 (a); order.\n   208\t- D12/D13: no clock.\n   209\t- D163: English product text.\n   210\t- D690: poc-v118 stays the product.\n   211\t- D261: the ruler is untouched.\n   212\t- D274: the extraction prompt is frozen.\n   213\t\n   214\t## 6. Tests (`tests/test_release.py`) and mutants\n   215\t\n   216\tThe fixtures use a real store on a temporary path (`store.create_view`, `store.insert`), with a real items database. Each test names\n   217\tits row above:\n   218\t1. **Closed set (§1).**\n   219\t   - Every dict in a fixture export has exactly its type's keys.\n   220\t   - Positive control: an export with one added key fails `check_export`.\n   221\t2. **Number with `lo`/`hi`.** The record carries the marker. No rung label, condition, `reasons`, `why_changed` or `implied_outcome` of\n   222\t   that view appears in any decoded package field.\n   223\t3. **Branch fixtures for identity and the report:**\n   224\t   - a condition-only number that resolves: `number`, and absent from `withheld_unresolved`;\n   225\t   - an unresolved number with a key: `number`, and present;\n   226\t   - an unresolved number without a key: `number`, and present.\n   227\t4. **Yes/No with numeric bounds** (`growth_rate` key, labels Yes/No): `yes_no`, with its answer label. A `why_changed` quoting\n   228\t   \"$1 trillion\" is absent.\n   229\t5. **Event with the served ledger's `v49` labels,** \"Restriction adopted\" / \"No restriction adopted\": `event`, with its label kept. A\n   230\t   `why_changed` quoting another question's band is absent.\n   231\t6. **Legacy store** with no `view_keys` table and `是`/`否` labels: `yes_no`.\n   232\t7. **Closing switch** whose reason names the band label: `open: false`, and the reason is absent.\n   233\t8. **Replacement and source visibility** at two bounds. A visible source with a missing item is refused.\n   234\t9. **Package:**\n   235\t   - staged, then checked, passes;\n   236\t   - a foreign file fails, and so does a subdirectory;\n   237\t   - a changed data byte fails;\n   238\t   - an extra manifest key with an unchanged data hash fails;\n   239\t   - a manifest `as_of` differing from the data's fails;\n   240\t   - an existing `--out` or staging folder is refused.\n   241\t10. **Origin check.** In a staged copy, the system's forecast text placed in an evidence `one_line` fails `check_origins`, naming the\n   242\t    field.\n   243\t11. **Builder end to end,** run as the user calls it (subprocess, `--as-of` omitted). The package is final and passes `check`. A\n   244\t    build on a store with a missing source item exits non-zero and leaves neither `--out` nor its staging folder.\n   245\t12. **Bound validation:** `2026-08-99` refused; a valid day before the first question gives an empty package.\n   246\t\n   247\t**Mutants,** on a scratch copy with `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`; each must fail a test:\n   248\t- `condition` emitted on number records;\n   249\t- `one_line` taken from the latest judgement's `why_changed`;\n   250\t- the event test removed;\n   251\t- the Yes/No test removed;\n   252\t- `check_package` without the file-set check;\n   253\t- manifest keys unchecked;\n   254\t- `check_export` without the closed-key check;\n   255\t- `check_origins` skipping evidence fields;\n   256\t- the switch reason emitted;\n   257\t- the missing-item refusal replaced by the id fallback.\n   258\t\n   259\t## 7. The $0 release check (stored stores, read-only)\n   260\t\n   261\tStores: `old-1`, `old-2`, `old-3` (`comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-N/prod/views.sqlite`, items `items-comparison.sqlite`) and the\n   262\tserved ledger with its items database.\n   263\t\n   264\t**Budgets,** set before the first control (AGENTS §2):\n   265\t- the package's data bytes at most `bundle.library`'s JSON bytes on the same store and bound;\n   266\t- export plus all checks at most three times `bundle.library`'s seconds on the same store, and at most 120 s per store.\n   267\t\n   268\tThe steps:\n   269\t1. **Build each store's package at its default bound.** The build passes `check_package` with `check_origins`. Report the fields\n   270\t   compared, the counts per class and the unresolved list.\n   271\t2. **The decisive acceptance case** (council 74), on the `old-1` package:\n   272\t   - Morningstar's `$361 billion` estimate (`e2295`) is kept, its summary and quote equal to the stored ones;\n   273\t   - the genuine \"Bullish confirmation\" quote (`e1865`) is kept;\n   274\t   - the genuine analyst \"$390 billion\" quote (`e3597`) is kept, as the control;\n   275\t   - in a copy of the staged package, the system's `old-1` j1580 `implied_outcome` (\"About $390 billion…\") substituted into\n   276\t     `e2295`'s summary fails `check_origins`;\n   277\t   - the same text added to the manifest fails `check_package`.\n   278\t3. **`old-1/v8`:** `class` is `number`, with the marker and the same evidence ids as `service.evidence` at the bound.\n   279\t4. **The known event leaks at their own dates.** Export `old-3` at 2026-08-25 (`v36` j799 is the latest judgement) and `old-1` at\n   280\t   2026-08-28 (`v10` j865). Each keeps its original answer label, and j799's \"around $1 trillion\" text and j865's band text are absent.\n   281\t5. **Control:** one unchanged event question keeps its label and evidence.\n   282\t6. **Closing.** On a temporary copy of `old-1`, add a closing switch for `v8` in the store's own format (\"due …, frozen on … at\n   283\t   rung N <label>\"). First confirm that `bundle.view_bundle` exposes the reason with the band label. Then confirm the package shows\n   284\t   `open: false` and not the reason.\n   285\t7. **Diagnostics** (not the gate). For every question, take each string the package must not hold:\n   286\t   - rung labels and conditions;\n   287\t   - judgement `reasons`, `why_changed`, `implied_outcome` and `reference`;\n   288\t   - switch reasons.\n   289\t\n   290\t   Search every decoded string field of the package for each, with no floor. List every hit with its question, field, evidence id\n   291\t   and the stored string it matched, and read each by hand. A genuine source quote, such as `e1865`'s \"Bullish\", is recorded as such.\n   292\t8. **Budgets:** bytes and seconds against the budgets above.\n   293\t\n   294\t## 8. A disclosed property, not built: evidence summaries keep extraction's wording\n   295\t\n   296\tThe release shows each evidence summary as extraction stored it; the release computes or converts nothing. A summary can make\n   297\tcontext explicit or restate a source figure by arithmetic, attributed to its source: `old-1/e3238` gives \"more than $40 billion in\n   298\tFY2028\" for a quote's \"more than double that next year\".\n   299\t- **Measured:** 25.6%, 25.2% and 25.4% of evidence in force in `old-1`, `old-2` and `old-3`, and 35.0% in the served ledger, carry a\n   300\t  number not in their quote. In a sample of 24, 23 are context: a year, a date, a quarter, a product name, an amount from the previous\n   301\t  sentence. One restates \"close to doubling\" as \"nearly 100%\".\n   302\t- **Why this is not the forecast D726 withholds.** Extraction never sees the system's forecast. Its request lists each open question\n   303\t  only as id, object, due day, question and a \"takes\" line (`placement.py:19-61`, `extraction.py:398-400`); no rung, label or\n   304\t  judged position.\n   305\t- **Disputed in council 74** (`claude-r74.md`). If the dispute stands, the cheaper, reversible course is taken: keep the stored\n   306\t  summary. A later version can drop the field from the allow-list.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
