{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba README.md | sed -n '88,118p'; rg -n 'current position|open questions.*ladder|shown.*rungs|rungs.*shown|prompt.*v18|v18.*prompt' docs/DECISIONS-log.md | head -35\"","aggregated_output":"    88\t\n    89\tThe default backend reads these local files:\n    90\t\n    91\t| Purpose | Path |\n    92\t|---|---|\n    93\t| Collected thesis ledger | `poc/data/served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite` |\n    94\t| Source items | `poc/data/items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite` (cleaned pages, D351, with the whole pages as fetched in column `text_page`; also kept apart in `items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.page.sqlite`) |\n    95\t| Replay configuration | `poc/config/poc-v118.json` (D370): v108 extraction, matching and judging settings without seeded starting questions or separate report import |\n    96\t| Idea configuration | `poc/config/poc-v118-idea.json`: two discovery calls and a final adoption/weighting call |\n    97\t| Derived service index and Idea archive | `poc/data/service-english/` by default; overridable per run |\n    98\t\n    99\t`poc/data/` is excluded from Git. A fresh clone includes the standalone demo, not these databases. Use the [data manifest](docs/research/2026-10-25-english/data-manifest.md) to locate preserved runs, or supply your own files with the documented CLI options. Keep provider credentials in the owner-only local file `~/.config/hivemind/credentials.json`, outside the repository.\n   100\t\n   101\t### Switching the served data\n   102\t\n   103\tThe page build, the two services and Compose each carry the same two defaults: the thesis ledger (`views.sqlite`) and the items database the ledger's input ids come from. Swap both together; a ledger whose items are missing shows evidence without titles or sources. Serve a copy of a ledger a run may still write (`snapshot.sh` in a run folder makes one with SQLite's backup API), never the file the run writes. The places that name the defaults, all changed in one edit:\n   104\t\n   105\t| Place | What to change |\n   106\t|---|---|\n   107\t| `scripts/mock_build.py` | `--ledger` and `--items` defaults, then `python3 scripts/mock_build.py` rebuilds `poc/mock/index.html` |\n   108\t| `scripts/hivemind_api.py` | `--views` and `--items` defaults |\n   109\t| `scripts/hivemind_mcp.py` | `--views` and `--items` defaults |\n   110\t| `docker-compose.yml` | the `/data/ledger` and `/data/items/items-window.sqlite` volumes of both services |\n   111\t| This README and `poc/ui/README.md` | the default paths named in the table above and in the build description |\n   112\t| `tests/test_ui_bundles.py` | `SERVED_VIEWS` and `SERVED_GROUPS`, the served library's thesis and group counts |\n   113\t\n   114\tThen restart the API in a new dated service folder (below) so the search index is built for the new ledger. The current default, `served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828`, is the three-month NVDA run (`poc-v34`, extraction v18) stopped and sealed at 2026-08-28 on evidence bloat (D358); its folder README names the one empty thesis removed.\n   115\t\n   116\t## Run the service for testing\n   117\t\n   118\tRun test services on the host. Start with read-only browsing and lexical search, which need no model or embedding calls. In the same shell where `repo` names the checkout, create a fresh dated run directory for the log, PID and derived files:\n2575:- Amendment, 2026-10-27 23:20: Alex stopped the restarted run (\"我不是要你看下step 1抽取到底行不行？\") and asked for the prompt to be read and fixed, with examples (\"什么叫重要陈述，你也没给例子\"). Arms B1–B6 ([log](research/2026-10-27-single-call/log.md) §10–17) rewrote the role as the model reads it: evidence first; four kinds of material statement with examples; a walk over the whole page (\"a page with eight such statements yields eight evidence items\"); a reject list with examples; links decided statement by statement; a rumour bears on a thesis as a confirmed statement does; T8's reading block narrowed to forecasts, ratings, targets and cited figures. Extraction v18 (`role-v18.txt`, `categories-v18.json`, `poc-v34.json`) supersedes v16 as the candidate configuration: on six articles sent five times each every material statement is present in every send; at scale (243 items of the run, one send each) 2% of answers are empty against 32% under v12 and 7–8 material statements come out per page, of which the theses that exist absorb 18% in the first week and 48% in the last. v17 and the two-call design stay refuted and unbuilt. The restarted run (`english-v32-nvda-3m-2026-10-27`, $0.215, 119 items) is paused; whether a run resumes, and with poc-v34, is Alex's call.\n2628:- Decided: `store.views_for_prompt(themes=True)` lists every open theme thesis after the objects' own, in creation order; `extraction.shown_views` is the one owner of the shown list (the stream and the parallel runner both read it); the groups block prints only member ids the answer may link to. Gated on the prompt version (`THEMES_SHOWN_FROM = 19`): v18 requests are byte-for-byte as before.\n3054:- Proof (`proof-judging-v6.txt`, `proof-judging-v6b.txt`: the last stored judgement request of 14 theses of arm 4 draw 1 re-sent once each under v6 and read beside the stored v5 answers, about a cent): every answer names the reference and derives the implied outcome. Six rungs moved against the stored ones: non-GAAP gross margin 3 → 2 (Q1 reported 75% and Q2 guided 75% sit on the rung-2 boundary), 2027 hyperscaler capex 4 → 5 (management's own \"more than $1 trillion\"), China accelerator share 4 → 5 (share \"fallen to zero\"), China H200 authorization No → Yes (a reported plan to permit named firms and reported progress in reviews, six months before the deadline), Data Center revenue 2 → 3 ($355–360 billion derived from Q1 and the total-revenue proxy, below the $360 billion boundary), Blackwell+Rubin revenue 2 → 1 in the first send by annualising a two-year \"$1 trillion visibility\" figure to $545 billion, a part above its whole: clause (3)'s consistency check was added for it and the re-send gives rung 2 ($320–360 billion, a share of the Data Center segment). Total revenue stays at 3 with the arithmetic shown (H1 $172.6 billion from Q1 and the Q2 guide; $400 billion needs more than $227 billion in H2). Prompt 2,453 → 3,782 characters: the request defined neither what a rung means nor a reference and its \"established\" wording forced the defect; the two sentences that carried it were cut. Configuration `poc-v90` (poc-v89 with judging-v6); the default stays `poc-v69`. Tests: `tests/test_stance_fields.py`. Measured by re-sent stored requests, not by an arm (Alex: \"不要再跑这些有的没的臂了\").\n9270:  - The ladder step's quoted reference text is stripped from the rungs shown to readers. The rungs' bounds and conditions are otherwise unchanged.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'served.*v49|v49.*Restriction|e3238|v18.*rung' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers --type md | head -30\"","aggregated_output":"docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.md:10:| `old-1/v15/e3238` | The quote gives **$20 billion** this year and **“more than double”** next year. The system’s one-line summary supplies **“more than $40 billion.”** That is faithful arithmetic, but the system wrote the dollar figure. |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.md:33:- **Tests 3, 4, 5, 6 and 11** need fixtures that distinguish the branches. Defaulting to `number` passes test 3 even if the unresolved report lists every number question. Assert a condition-only *resolved* question is absent from that report and an unresolved one is present, both with and without a key. For test 6 use the served ledger’s `v49` labels, **“Restriction adopted” / “No restriction adopted.”** All 85 comparison-store events also have Yes/No labels, so removing event recognition can leave the displayed answer unchanged. Exercise the legacy case with the key table genuinely absent. [Tests:168](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:168) · [Event overlap:85](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:85) · [Legacy lookup:159](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/store.py:159)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:229:5. **Event with the served ledger's `v49` labels,** \"Restriction adopted\" / \"No restriction adopted\": `event`, with its label kept. A\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:297:context explicit or restate a source figure by arithmetic, attributed to its source: `old-1/e3238` gives \"more than $40 billion in\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r74.md:34:`codex-r74.md` §1 asks the release to use the source wording where a summary introduces a calculated figure (`e3238`: \"more than\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
