{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3,re,json,collections\ndb=sqlite3.connect(\\\"file:poc/data/sealed-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/archive.sqlite?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\",uri=True)\nforms=collections.Counter(); odd=[]\nfor cid,req in db.execute(\\\"select call_id,request_json from model_calls where purpose=?\\\",(\\\"extract\\\",)):\n s=json.loads(req)[\\\"messages\\\"][-1][\\\"content\\\"];pre=s.partition(\\\"[Item]\\\")[0];q=pre.partition(\\\"[Existing theses of these objects]\\\")[2].partition(\\\"[Research groups]\\\")[0];v=[l for l in q.splitlines() if l.startswith(\\\"  - \\\")]; forms[\\\"requests\\\"]+=1; forms[\\\"with_theses\\\"]+=bool(v);forms[\\\"lines\\\"]+=len(v)\n for l in v:\n  if not re.fullmatch(r\\\"  - v\\\\d+ \\\\(.+?, focus .+, due [\"'^)]*'\"\\\\): .+\\\",l): odd.append((cid,l[:180]))\n if re.search(r\\\"\"'^'\"\\\\s*(?:rung|current position|judgement|selected label)\\\\s*[:=]\\\",pre,re.M|re.I): forms[\\\"explicit\\\"]+=1\nprint(forms,len(odd),odd[:2])'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3,re,json,collections\ndb=sqlite3.connect(\\\"file:poc/data/sealed-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/archive.sqlite?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\",uri=True)\nforms=collections.Counter(); odd=[]\nfor cid,req in db.execute(\\\"select call_id,request_json from model_calls where purpose=?\\\",(\\\"extract\\\",)):\n s=json.loads(req)[\\\"messages\\\"][-1][\\\"content\\\"];pre=s.partition(\\\"[Item]\\\")[0];q=pre.partition(\\\"[Existing theses of these objects]\\\")[2].partition(\\\"[Research groups]\\\")[0];v=[l for l in q.splitlines() if l.startswith(\\\"  - \\\")]; forms[\\\"requests\\\"]+=1; forms[\\\"with_theses\\\"]+=bool(v);forms[\\\"lines\\\"]+=len(v)\n for l in v:\n  if not re.fullmatch(r\\\"  - v\\\\d+ \\\\(.+?, focus .+, due [\"'^)]*'\"\\\\): .+\\\",l): odd.append((cid,l[:180]))\n if re.search(r\\\"\"'^'\"\\\\s*(?:rung|current position|judgement|selected label)\\\\s*[:=]\\\",pre,re.M|re.I): forms[\\\"explicit\\\"]+=1\nprint(forms,len(odd),odd[:2])'\"","aggregated_output":"Counter({'lines': 43895, 'requests': 1819, 'with_theses': 1806}) 0 []\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '58,132p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/vocabulary.py | sed -n '14,36p'; rg -n 'before.*check|staging|atomic|rename' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/{claude-r74.md,RELEASE-BUILD.md}\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '58,132p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/vocabulary.py | sed -n '14,36p'; rg -n 'before.*check|staging|atomic|rename' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/{claude-r74.md,RELEASE-BUILD.md}\"","aggregated_output":"    58\t  | manifest | `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`, `data_sha256` |\n    59\t\n    60\t- **`question_class(views_db, view_id, labels)`** (design §3):\n    61\t  - `event` when the view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES`. The key is read as `select measure from view_keys`, and\n    62\t    only when the table exists;\n    63\t  - `yes_no` when there are exactly two labels which, through `vocabulary.canonical('label', …)`, are `Yes` and `No` in either order;\n    64\t  - `number` otherwise: a view with no key, or one whose bands cannot be resolved.\n    65\t- **`release_export(views_db, items_db, as_of=None)`:**\n    66\t  - pins both connections (`bundle.read_snapshot`);\n    67\t  - resolves the bound with `service.resolve_bound`, refuses a store with no default day, and validates the bound with\n    68\t    `date.fromisoformat`;\n    69\t  - exports every view that exists at the bound (`service.view_exists`), closed ones included, in `created_seq` order;\n    70\t  - builds each record field by field from the table above, with column-limited SQL:\n    71\t    - `select view_id, question, created_seq from views`;\n    72\t    - `select position, label from rungs`;\n    73\t    - `select rung from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day<=? order by judgement_id desc limit 1`;\n    74\t    - `service.is_open_as_of`, which reads only `open` and `after_seq`;\n    75\t  - takes evidence in force from `service.evidence` and its fields from that record;\n    76\t  - looks up each source's `title`, `publisher` and `source_uri` in the items database by `input_id`. A visible source whose item is\n    77\t    missing raises `ReleaseRefused` (there is no fallback to the id);\n    78\t  - calls `check_export` on its own result before returning (AGENTS §3: the writer refuses).\n    79\t- **`check_export(data)`:** the closed-set check.\n    80\t  - Every dict at every level has exactly its record type's keys.\n    81\t  - Value checks:\n    82\t    - `format` and `allow_list` equal the constants, and `as_of` is an ISO date;\n    83\t    - `class` is in its set;\n    84\t    - a number record's `forecast` is the marker;\n    85\t    - `answers` is two strings, and `answer` is one of them or null;\n    86\t    - `open` is a bool and every text field is a string.\n    87\t  - It returns the counts it judged: questions per class, evidence, sources.\n    88\t- **`check_origins(views_db, items_db, data)`:** the pass condition. It is independent of the exporter's code path and compares every\n    89\t  field with its permitted stored source at the package's `as_of`, by direct SQL:\n    90\t  - the question set equals the views visible at the bound, with `question` equal to `views.question`;\n    91\t  - `open` equals the latest visible switch's `open`;\n    92\t  - for `event` and `yes_no`: `answers` equal the rung labels in position order, and `answer` equals the label of the latest judgement\n    93\t    rung on or before the bound, or null;\n    94\t  - for `number`: only the marker;\n    95\t  - the evidence id set equals the links visible at the bound, minus those whose latest replacement is visible, computed in its own\n    96\t    SQL. Each evidence field equals the `evidence` row's column. Each source list equals the visible `evidence_sources` rows joined to\n    97\t    `items` (`title`, `publisher`, `source_uri`, `publication_day`).\n    98\t\n    99\t  Any difference raises `ReleaseRefused`, naming the question, the field and the evidence id. It returns the number of fields\n   100\t  compared.\n   101\t- **`write_package(data, out_dir)`:**\n   102\t  - refuses an existing `out_dir`, and also an existing `<out_dir>.staging`, left by a crash, which the user removes;\n   103\t  - writes `release-data.json` and `manifest.json` into `<out_dir>.staging`;\n   104\t  - returns the staged path. It does not move it.\n   105\t- **`check_package(path, views_db=None, items_db=None)`:**\n   106\t  - the directory holds exactly `PACKAGE_FILES`, with no subdirectories;\n   107\t  - the manifest has exactly its four keys, and its `format`, `allow_list` and `as_of` equal the data's;\n   108\t  - its sha256 equals the data file's;\n   109\t  - the data passes `check_export`, and, when the stores are given, `check_origins`;\n   110\t  - it returns the counts.\n   111\t- **`withheld_unresolved(views_db, data)`** is for the report only. It lists the number questions whose `service.ladder_bands(rungs)`\n   112\t  returns `(None, reason)`, with the reason and whether the view has a key. Its output never enters the package.\n   113\t\n   114\t`scripts/release_build.py`:\n   115\t- **`build --ledger --items [--as-of] --out`:**\n   116\t  1. `release_export`;\n   117\t  2. `write_package` to the staging folder;\n   118\t  3. `check_package` on the staged folder, with the stores;\n   119\t  4. on success, rename the staging folder to `--out`, then write `<out>.report.json` beside it (via a temporary file and rename);\n   120\t  5. on `ReleaseRefused`, remove the staging folder it created, print the reason and exit non-zero. No final folder exists.\n   121\t\n   122\t  It has no input path for prepared or translated JSON, and it takes no clock reading; the folder name is the caller's (D12, D13).\n   123\t- **`check <out> --ledger --items`:** re-runs `check_package` with the stores on an existing package and rewrites\n   124\t  `<out>.report.json`. This is also the retry after a report write failed.\n   125\t- **The report:**\n   126\t  - the store path and the bound;\n   127\t  - counts per class;\n   128\t  - the unresolved list;\n   129\t  - the fields compared;\n   130\t  - bytes and seconds.\n   131\t\n   132\t## 2. State × event (one export, read-only)\n    14\tASSET_LABELS = ['Strongly bullish', 'Bullish', 'Neutral', 'Bearish', 'Strongly bearish']\n    15\tYES_NO = ['Yes', 'No']\n    16\t\n    17\tLEGACY = {\n    18\t    'kind': {'对象观点': 'asset', '主题观点': 'theme'},\n    19\t    'tier': {'发生的事': 'fact', '当事人说的': 'party_statement', '第三方看法': 'third_party_view', '传闻': 'rumour'},\n    20\t    'candidate_outcome': {'归入已有的': 'merge', '接续': 'succession', '新观点': 'new', '不开': 'skip'},\n    21\t    'evidence_outcome': {'重复': 'repeat', '替代': 'replace', '新证据': 'new'},\n    22\t    'push': {'推向第一格': 'toward_first', '推向最后一格': 'toward_last', '不推': 'none'},\n    23\t    'direction': {'对方第一格是看多': 'first_is_bullish', '对方最后一格是看多': 'last_is_bullish', '同向': 'same', '反向': 'opposite'},\n    24\t    'label': {'强烈看多': 'Strongly bullish', '看多': 'Bullish', '中性': 'Neutral', '看空': 'Bearish', '强烈看空': 'Strongly bearish', '是': 'Yes', '否': 'No'},\n    25\t}\n    26\t\n    27\t\n    28\tdef canonical(field, value):\n    29\t    \"\"\"The canonical value of a closed field: a legacy value converted, a canonical one kept, anything else unchanged.\"\"\"\n    30\t    if not isinstance(value, str):\n    31\t        return value\n    32\t    return LEGACY[field].get(value.strip(), value)\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\tdef legacy(field, value):\n    36\t    \"\"\"The Chinese spelling of a canonical value, for a request built for a Chinese prompt version.\"\"\"\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:102:  - refuses an existing `out_dir`, and also an existing `<out_dir>.staging`, left by a crash, which the user removes;\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:103:  - writes `release-data.json` and `manifest.json` into `<out_dir>.staging`;\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:117:  2. `write_package` to the staging folder;\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:119:  4. on success, rename the staging folder to `--out`, then write `<out>.report.json` beside it (via a temporary file and rename);\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:120:  5. on `ReleaseRefused`, remove the staging folder it created, print the reason and exit non-zero. No final folder exists.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:151:| `--out` exists, or `<out>.staging` exists | refused before any write | nothing | — |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:152:| `check_export`, `check_package` or `check_origins` refuses | the staging folder is removed, exit non-zero | nothing final | — |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:153:| Crash while staging | the staging folder is left, and the next build refuses until it is removed | staging only | — |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:154:| Crash after the rename, before the report | the package is final and checked; `check` rewrites the report | package | — |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:173:| `answers`, `answer` | `rungs.label` by position; the latest `judgements.rung` on or before the bound | `check_origins` |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:240:   - an existing `--out` or staging folder is refused.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:244:    build on a store with a missing source item exits non-zero and leaves neither `--out` nor its staging folder.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r74.md:12:3. **The staged package is checked before the rename.** A refused build removes its own staging folder and leaves no final folder. A\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r74.md:13:   crash leaves the staging folder, and the next build refuses until it is removed. A `check` mode re-verifies an existing package and\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_49","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3\ndb=sqlite3.connect(\\\"file:poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\",uri=True)\nfor i in [\\\"e2295\\\",\\\"e1865\\\",\\\"e3597\\\"]:\n print(i,db.execute(\\\"select r.old_evidence_id from replacements r where old_evidence_id=?\\\",(i,)).fetchall())\nprint(db.execute(\\\"select max(publication_day) from judgements\\\").fetchone())\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
