{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3,glob,re\nnum=lambda s:{n.replace(\\\",\\\",\\\"\\\").rstrip(\\\".\\\").lstrip(\\\"0\\\") or \\\"0\\\" for n in re.findall(r\\\"\\\\d+(?:[.,]\\\\d+)*\\\",s)}\nfor p in sorted(glob.glob(\\\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-*/prod/views.sqlite\\\"))+glob.glob(\\\"poc/data/served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite\\\"):\n d=sqlite3.connect(\\\"file:\\\"+p+\\\"?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\",uri=True); bound=d.execute(\\\"select max(day) from days_completed\\\").fetchone()[0] or d.execute(\\\"select max(publication_day) from judgements\\\").fetchone()[0];d.row_factory=sqlite3.Row; seq={r[0]:r[1] for r in d.execute(\\\"select sequence_no,min(publication_day) from processing_steps where sequence_no>0 group by 1\\\")};seq[0]=min(seq.values());vis=lambda s:s in seq and seq[s]<=bound;keys=dict(d.execute(\\\"select view_id,measure from view_keys\\\")); labs={}; [labs.setdefault(vid,[]).append(s) for vid,s in d.execute(\\\"select view_id,label from rungs\\\")]; ns={v for v,s in d.execute(\\\"select view_id,created_seq from views\\\") if vis(s) and keys.get(v) not in (\\\"event\\\",\\\"policy_event\\\") and sorted({\\\"是\\\":\\\"Yes\\\",\\\"否\\\":\\\"No\\\"}.get(z,z) for z in labs[v])\"'!=[\"No\",\"Yes\"]}; rep={i:s for i,s in d.execute(\"select old_evidence_id,seq from replacements order by id\")};ids={e for e,v,s in d.execute(\"select evidence_id,view_id,seq from evidence_links\") if v in ns and vis(s) and not vis(rep.get(e))};n=sum(bool(num(s)-num(q)) for e,s,q in d.execute(\"select evidence_id,one_line,quote from evidence\") if e in ids);print(p,bound,len(ns),n,len(ids))'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3,glob,re\nnum=lambda s:{n.replace(\\\",\\\",\\\"\\\").rstrip(\\\".\\\").lstrip(\\\"0\\\") or \\\"0\\\" for n in re.findall(r\\\"\\\\d+(?:[.,]\\\\d+)*\\\",s)}\nfor p in sorted(glob.glob(\\\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-*/prod/views.sqlite\\\"))+glob.glob(\\\"poc/data/served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite\\\"):\n d=sqlite3.connect(\\\"file:\\\"+p+\\\"?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\",uri=True); bound=d.execute(\\\"select max(day) from days_completed\\\").fetchone()[0] or d.execute(\\\"select max(publication_day) from judgements\\\").fetchone()[0];d.row_factory=sqlite3.Row; seq={r[0]:r[1] for r in d.execute(\\\"select sequence_no,min(publication_day) from processing_steps where sequence_no>0 group by 1\\\")};seq[0]=min(seq.values());vis=lambda s:s in seq and seq[s]<=bound;keys=dict(d.execute(\\\"select view_id,measure from view_keys\\\")); labs={}; [labs.setdefault(vid,[]).append(s) for vid,s in d.execute(\\\"select view_id,label from rungs\\\")]; ns={v for v,s in d.execute(\\\"select view_id,created_seq from views\\\") if vis(s) and keys.get(v) not in (\\\"event\\\",\\\"policy_event\\\") and sorted({\\\"是\\\":\\\"Yes\\\",\\\"否\\\":\\\"No\\\"}.get(z,z) for z in labs[v])\"'!=[\"No\",\"Yes\"]}; rep={i:s for i,s in d.execute(\"select old_evidence_id,seq from replacements order by id\")};ids={e for e,v,s in d.execute(\"select evidence_id,view_id,seq from evidence_links\") if v in ns and vis(s) and not vis(rep.get(e))};n=sum(bool(num(s)-num(q)) for e,s,q in d.execute(\"select evidence_id,one_line,quote from evidence\") if e in ids);print(p,bound,len(ns),n,len(ids))'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite 2026-09-20 19 1235 4761\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/views.sqlite 2026-09-20 17 1104 4255\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-3/prod/views.sqlite 2026-09-20 18 1194 4494\npoc/data/served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite 2026-08-28 13 1093 2919\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_51","type":"agent_message","text":"**Verdict: not ready to build.** The revised check would catch Hivemind’s $390 billion forecast substituted into Morningstar’s summary. It could still certify `old-1` as current through September 21, although the store’s last completed day is September 20. It could also certify `old-1/v10` with its real “Yes” answer replaced by “Forecast unavailable.” Both errors survive because the checker takes the date and question type from the package it is checking. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:88](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:88) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:172](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:172) · [service.py:64](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:64)\n\n### 1. Accepted round-74 findings\n\n| Finding | Revision 2 |\n|---|---|\n| Origin check and decisive case | **The decisive case is resolved.** I verified the three genuine records in `old-1`. `e2295` quotes Morningstar’s $361 billion, `e1865` contains “Bullish confirmation,” and `e3597` quotes analysts’ $390 billion. The design keeps all three, rejects j1580 substituted into `e2295`, and rejects the same text added as a manifest field. The string search is now diagnostic. The broader origin check remains incomplete as described below. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:269](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:269) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:285](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:285) |\n| Missing item, manifest, date and narrow reads | **Resolved on the export path.** A missing source item refuses the build. The manifest has four required fields, with agreement on the date, versions and data hash. The exporter validates the resolved date and distinguishes a missing default from a valid empty day. Its own queries read rung labels and positions, the selected rung and the measure. The report correctly unpacks `(bands, reason)`. The separate `check` path still needs the date and missing-item checks below. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:60](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:60) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:105](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:105) |\n| Build order, retry and budgets | **The order and thresholds are resolved.** The builder checks staging before rename. A report-only failure can be retried against the finished package. Size and time now have thresholds fixed before the first control. A retry can measure its own verification time, but cannot recover the elapsed time of the original export. Its report must distinguish those measurements. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:115](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:115) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:264](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:264) |\n| Tests and mutants | **The identity fixtures and dated leak cases are resolved.** The design now distinguishes resolved and unresolved numbers, a genuinely absent key table, and an event with distinctive labels. August 25 and August 28 select the intended judgements. **The builder refusal test remains open.** Test 10 calls the checker directly. Test 11 fails on a missing item *before staging exists*. Both can pass if the builder stops checking staged files before rename. Exercise the builder with a staged origin mismatch and assert nonzero exit, no final package, and removal of its own staging directory. Removing the builder’s check must fail that test. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:223](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:223) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:241](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:241) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:279](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:279) |\n\nThe four scope choices are carried through. The first package omits `object`, `kind` and groups. Idea submission is deferred, its acceptance remains pending, and there is no minimum length for diagnostic matches. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:28](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:28) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:51](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:51) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:290](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:290)\n\n### 2. Disputed evidence summaries\n\n**Claude is right about what the production extraction request sees.** For an existing question, it sends the ID, object, due day, question and a description of what evidence belongs there. It sends no stored rung, rung label or judged position. The response schema asks the model to *write* labels for newly proposed questions. `research_context.Reader` really does load stored rungs and the latest judgement, but its expanded record is not sent by `extraction.read_item`. I also checked the historical archive because the served ledger used extraction v18. Across its 1,819 extraction requests, the 43,895 displayed thesis lines contained the ID, object, focus, due day and question. [placement.py:19](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/placement.py:19) · [placement.py:59](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/placement.py:59) · [extraction.py:399](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/extraction.py:399) · [extraction.py:88](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/extraction.py:88) · [extraction.py:460](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/extraction.py:460) · [research_context.py:49](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/research_context.py:49) · [research_context.py:95](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/research_context.py:95) · [README.md:114](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/README.md:114)\n\n**The census percentages reproduce.** The counts are 1,379/5,390, 1,284/5,102, 1,386/5,447 and 1,470/4,199. They measure extra digit sequences across distinct evidence records linked to **all** question types. A year, `H200`, and a calculated dollar amount all count. The sample was six flagged records per store. This supplies evidence against filtering every numeric mismatch. It does not measure how often a summary attributes a calculated amount to a source. [oneline_census.py:5](/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/oneline_census.py:5) · [oneline_census.py:18](/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/oneline_census.py:18) · [claude-r74.md:42](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r74.md:42)\n\n**I still disagree on “amounts as quoted.”** Keeping `e3238` does not disclose a D726 judgement. But I read the underlying article: it says `$20 billion` and “more than double that next year.” The stored summary says **NVIDIA projected more than $40 billion**. The arithmetic is faithful. The attributed dollar figure is extraction’s wording. Revision 4 explicitly requires “amounts as quoted,” so I would use the source wording for that amount. The disagreement is narrow and does not justify a digit filter or a change to extraction. Under the stated council fallback, keeping the stored summary is the cheaper reversible course, with this exception recorded. This dispute is separate from the build blockers. [FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:47](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:47) · [DECISIONS-log.md:11004](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11004) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:296](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:296)\n\n### 3. Remaining build blockers\n\n1. **Derive the expected date, class and records independently.** During build, compare the packaged date with the requested or resolved day. During `check`, pass the package date through the store’s completed-day check. I verified that `old-1` ends September 20 and has no later processing or judgement rows, so merely comparing its contents at September 21 detects nothing. Derive each question’s class from the stored measure and labels before selecting its permitted fields. Compare record counts as well as IDs, since a set comparison accepts a duplicate question or evidence record. These checks belong in the pass condition for each package. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:88](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:88) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:172](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:172) · [service.py:57](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:57)\n2. **Make a missing source item refuse `check`, too.** Start from every visible `evidence_sources` row and require a matching item for each one. An ordinary inner join silently drops a missing item. A package omitting that same source would then agree with the checker. Test this through `check` using an existing package and item store with one referenced item missing. Take the source day from `evidence_sources`, as the value table specifies. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:95](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:95) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:176](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:176) · [service.py:230](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:230)\n3. **Check the files the reader will actually receive.** Two permitted filenames and “no subdirectories” still allow a symbolic link to data outside the package. Checking the keys of a parsed dictionary also misses duplicate JSON member names: a file can physically carry two `one_line` values while the parser compares only the last. Require two regular, non-symlink files and reject duplicate JSON member names in both files. These are properties of the finished package that the new `check` command can verify. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:79](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:79) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:105](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:105) · [FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:37](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:37)\n4. **Give staging one owner through rename.** The table treats an existing staging directory as crash debris, although another build may still be checking it. Specify exclusive staging creation, cleanup only by the invocation that acquired it, and a final move that refuses an existing destination. An ordinary write or rename error also needs a defined outcome. Test two builds aimed at the same output: the losing build must leave the winner’s staging and finished package intact. After a report-only failure, `check` should leave the checked package in place and report only the measurements it can reproduce. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:101](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:101) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:119](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:119) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:150](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:150)\n5. **Make the four-store acceptance runnable.** Step 7 asks for `judgements.implied_outcome` and `reference` on every store. I checked the served ledger’s actual schema. It has neither column. Read the available diagnostic columns and report the two as absent on that ledger. Otherwise the specified acceptance can fail on a valid package before it finishes. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:261](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:261) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:285](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:285) · [store.py:152](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/store.py:152)\n\nThis was a read-only design review. I verified the stored examples, request path, schemas and census. No release implementation or acceptance run exists yet."}}
